# Module Development Rules

## Module structure

```
modules/<mod-name>/
├── CMakeLists.txt
├── src/
│   ├── <mod>_loader.cpp      — AddSC entry point
│   └── <mod>.cpp/h           — Module logic
├── conf/
│   └── <mod>.conf.dist       — Default config
├── data/sql/
│   └── db_world/             — SQL updates
└── README.md
```

## CMake integration

```cmake
# Minimal CMakeLists.txt
add_module(
  NAME mod_name
  SOURCES
    src/mod_name_loader.cpp
    src/mod_name.cpp
  HEADERS
    src/mod_name.h
  MODULE_DEPS
    # List dependencies
)
```

## Module lifecycle hooks

| Hook | Method | When |
|---|---|---|
| Load | `OnLoad()` | Module loaded on startup |
| Unload | `OnUnload()` | Module unloaded on shutdown |
| Config | `OnConfigLoad()` | Config (re)loaded |
| WorldScript hooks | Various | Game events |

## Safety rules

1. **Don't modify core directly** — use hooks and ScriptObject registration
2. **Config files**: Ship `.conf.dist` with defaults; never modify core config
3. **SQL updates**: Follow same lifecycle as core SQL updates
4. **Dependencies**: Declare in CMakeLists.txt MODULE_DEPS
5. **Thread safety**: Module code runs on the world thread; use scheduled operations for async work
6. **Memory**: Clean up in `OnUnload()`
7. **Null checks**: All pointers from core API must be null-checked

